glossary.paragraph:
A matrix pair ﻿$(A,B)$ where $A$﻿ is $n \times n$, $B$﻿ has $n$﻿ rows, and $$\text{rank}\begin{bmatrix}
    B & {AB} & {A^{2}B} & \cdots & {A^{n - 1}B}
    \end{bmatrix} = n$$

The system of equations represented by $A^{T}A\textbf{x} = A^{T}\textbf{b}$, whose solution yields all least-squares solutions of $A\textbf{x} = \textbf{b}$. In statistics, a common notation is $\begin{array}{l}
    {X^{T}X\mathbf{\beta} = X^{T}\textbf{y}}
    \end{array}$.

An $n \times n$ matrix $V$ or its transpose, when $V$ has the form$$V = \,\,\begin{bmatrix}
    1 & x_{1} & x_{1}^{2} & \cdots & x_{1}^{n - 1} \\
    1 & x_{2} & x_{2}^{2} & \cdots & x_{2}^{n - 1} \\
     \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & & \vdots \\
    1 & x_{n} & x_{n}^{2} & \cdots & x_{n}^{n - 1}
    \end{bmatrix}$$
